       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't make it safe.\n\nThe 50 mg may be a typo. Usual adult dosing is:\n- **Starting dose:** 5 mg by mouth once daily. Use 2.5 mg if the patient is frail or elderly, or has hepatic impairment.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg by mouth once daily.\n\nTell me the dose you intended, for example 5 mg or 10 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 50 mg, please confirm that and give me the clinical reason. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
